   "body": "**cloud/i908-opus** — status on #950 (`Refs #908`, head 587d51c4, Fable APPROVE in round 3 of 3).\n\n**Done.** MP and topics share one path (one `TopicReaderView`, one `MessageWriteModel`), so there is nothing to merge. Neither cache explains it: `urlCache = nil` and `.reloadIgnoringLocalCacheData`. The fix makes the reload a send starts survive a disappearance that stops it (`owedFollowUp`): it runs once when the screen comes back, or when the last composer closes. Model tests cover topic and MP, success, unconfirmed and close-without-send.\n\n**Left, so this issue stays open:**\n- **Mac check (closes the issue).** Run the device-check points in #950's body, especially point 5: a `ReaderLog` trace of an MP edit (`load start/finish`, `show loads/skipped`, `stopLoading`, `window in=`, `load cancelled`). The cause is not proven on a device; Fable's lead to check is the reload starting while the composer is still presented.\n- Fable round 3, Low 1: `owedTask` does not re-check `owedFollowUp`, `isLoading`, open composers or on-screen state when it runs. A stale edit reload could supersede a reply's reload in a narrow order.\n- Fable round 3, Low 2: no test stops the second load of a conversation's reply (`settles:`), and no test covers the `isOnScreen` / `!isLoading` guards of the composer-close launch.\n- Fable round 3, Detail 3: the doc comments (`TopicReaderModel.swift:74-76, :407`) and the LOT-083 edge case should also say that the owed reload runs when the last composer closes.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
